I am sitting on the U-Bahn.
The train is quite full this evening.
But fortunately I have a seat.
The small bakery box rests safely on my lap.
I take the mobile phone in my hand.
I write Nele a short message.
I write to her that I will arrive in ten minutes.
Then I put the phone away again.
The U-Bahn travels right across the whole city.
Soon I reach the right stop and get off.
I walk up the stairs and emerge outside.
It is a beautiful evening in late spring.
The sun is still shining brightly and the air is pleasantly mild.
I do not really know this neighborhood yet.
I walk the last few streets to Nele's flat.
I once again carry the delicate box completely flat in both hands.
I hope that the dessert will taste good to Nele.
